<figure class="diagram">
    <div class="diagram-scroll">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 440 560" role="img" aria-labelledby="query-title query-desc">
            <title id="query-title">Life of a query</title>
            <desc id="query-desc">
                Planned query path. Analyze the text, search each segment and the memtable, merge the top hits.
                If there are fewer hits than requested, run the relaxation cascade and say what changed.
            </desc>
            <rect width="440" height="560" fill="#ffffff" />
            <g font-family="Courier New, Courier, monospace" font-size="14" fill="#000000">
                <rect x="70" y="16" width="300" height="56" fill="#c0c0c0" stroke="#000080" stroke-width="2" />
                <text x="86" y="48">1. Analyze the query text</text>

                <polygon points="220,80 210,100 230,100" fill="#000080" />

                <rect x="70" y="108" width="300" height="72" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#000080" stroke-width="2" />
                <text x="86" y="136">2. Search each segment</text>
                <text x="86" y="158">and the memtable</text>

                <polygon points="220,188 210,208 230,208" fill="#000080" />

                <rect x="70" y="216" width="300" height="56" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#000080" stroke-width="2" />
                <text x="86" y="248">3. Merge per-segment top hits</text>

                <polygon points="220,280 210,300 230,300" fill="#000080" />

                <rect x="40" y="308" width="360" height="72" fill="#ffffcc" stroke="#000080" stroke-width="2" />
                <text x="56" y="336">4. Fewer hits than min_results?</text>
                <text x="56" y="360">No: return them. Yes: relax.</text>

                <polygon points="220,388 210,408 230,408" fill="#000080" />

                <rect x="40" y="416" width="360" height="56" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#800000" stroke-width="2" />
                <text x="56" y="448">5. Relaxation cascade, L0 through L5</text>

                <text x="16" y="504">Filters stay strict unless the caller opts in.</text>
                <text x="16" y="528">The response names the level and the words that changed.</text>
                <text x="16" y="552">Planned. SPEC section 7. Milestones M7 and M8.</text>
            </g>
        </svg>
    </div>
    <figcaption>
        Planned query path (SPEC §7). Step 4 is the branch into zero-results relaxation.
    </figcaption>
</figure>
